WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/forms/FormField.tsx — an intentionally tiny, PRESENTATIONAL wrapper:
    <div space-y-1.5>
      <label htmlFor={fieldId} text-xs font-medium text-secondary> {label}
        {required && <span text-rose-300 aria-label="required">*</span>} </label>
      {children}                                                  // the control slot
      {error ? <p role="alert" text-xs text-rose-300>{error}</p>
             : hint ? <p text-xs text-muted>{hint}</p> : null}
  Hooks: only `useId` (generates the label↔control id). No charts, no maps, no data fetch.
  Render branches: required-or-not × (error | hint | neither); `error` strictly hides `hint`.
  i18n key extracted from the documented example: `alerts.signal` → "Signal" (+ the `aria-label="required"` word).
  Per the prompt's own "States" boilerplate (loading/empty/error/stale/offline): this leaf fetches nothing, so
  the data-lifecycle chrome is owned by the host form — only the inline validation state lives here (faithfully
  reproduced). This is the same boundary every presentational P4 leaf (ToolCard, SummaryStatsRow) documents.

