PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  <label> text-[var(--text-secondary)] text-xs font-medium  → Font.TS.label + Color.TS.textSecondary
  required <span text-rose-300> aria-label="required"       → "*" in Color.TS.statusDanger, hidden from VoiceOver;
                                                               required state folded into one spoken label ("Signal, required")
  <p role="alert" text-rose-300>{error}                     → Color.TS.statusDanger + .isStaticText trait +
                                                               AccessibilityNotification.Announcement on appear
  <p text-[var(--text-muted)]>{hint}                        → Font.TS.caption + Color.TS.textMuted
  useId (label↔control id)                                  → caller htmlFor ?? a stable generated id; .accessibilityIdentifier
  error ? : hint ? : null                                   → FormFieldProjection.resolve (pure, unit-tested)
  i18n      : label/hint/error are caller-localized props (web parity); the surface-owned "required" word + the
              documented `alerts.signal` key resolve through the P1/S10 facade — zero English literals in Swift.
  a11y      : VoiceOver label incl. required suffix · Dynamic Type (token scale + wrap, no truncation) ·
              reduce-motion honored (TSAnimation) · error announced (role="alert" parity).
  telemetry : view.opened surface="FormField" via FormFieldModel.start (P1/S11), default OSLog sink.

